Description:
  'A search for the production of three Higgs bosons ($HHH$) in the
  $b\bar{b}b\bar{b}b\bar{b}$ final state is presented.
  The search uses 126~$\text{fb}^{-1}$ of proton--proton collision data at 
  $\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV collected with the ATLAS detector at the Large Hadron Collider.
  The analysis targets both non-resonant and resonant production of $HHH$.
  The resonant interpretations primarily consider a cascade decay topology of 
  $X\rightarrow SH\rightarrow HHH$ with masses of the new scalars $X$ and $S$ up to 
  1.5 TeV and 1 TeV, respectively.
  In addition to scenarios where $S$ is off-shell, the non-resonant interpretation
  includes a search for standard model (SM) $HHH$ production, with limits on the 
  tri-linear and quartic Higgs self-coupling set.
  No evidence for $HHH$ production is observed.
  An upper limit of 59 fb is set, at 95\% confidence level, on the cross-section for
  Standard-Model $HHH$ production.'
ValidationInfo:
  'Normalised Neural network inputs outputs validated using Auxiliary Figures 2-13
  (not on hepdata, I used a clicker).
  Absolute bin-counts for a variety of mass-points validated using the Signal 
  distributions in the HS3 likelihood jsons. Distributions were consistently within 
  the "acceptable" 10-15% error range. Performance was slightly better in the SR (6b)
  than the CR (5b).
  See https://gitlab.com/apapaefs/twosinglet for information on generating param cards.
  All event generation carried out with MG5.
  See validation plots attached to Rivet MR !1110.
  Note that for cutflows etc, the ATLAS published results set the XS to a fixed 50 fb.
  ' 
